// A lost handshake ACK causes SYN-ACK retries after 300 and 600 ms gaps.
// The ACK at 1.0 s completes the handshake and stops retransmission.
// Data arrives at 2.3 s, past the 2.1 s deadline that would have sent
// another SYN-ACK without that ACK. The connection then echoes and closes.
// SYN-ACK retries collapse Cubic's window to one MSS, 1460 bytes;
// the later 10-byte echo fits that window.
// Window-update ACK after the handshake: the SYN-ACK window is unscaled, capped 65535;
// the scaled allowance, 90 frames x 1460 B capped by the 128 KiB buffer = 131072
// (32768 << 2), is >= 2 x 65535, so Zhida sends one pure window-update ACK.

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0.3  > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0.6  > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0.1  < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    > . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 32768
+1.3  < P. 1:11(10) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1:11(10) ack 11 win 32768
+0    < . 11:11(0) ack 11 win 502
+0    < F. 11:11(0) ack 11 win 502
+0    > . 11:11(0) ack 12 win 32768
+0    > F. 11:11(0) ack 12 win 32768
+0    < . 12:12(0) ack 12 win 502
